<figure class="snapshot" data-r46-snapshot aria-labelledby="r46-title">
 <figcaption id="r46-title"><span>Figure 1</span> A timestamp needs both a promise and its data</figcaption>
 <div class="controls"><label>Read at <select data-time><option value="100">100 · before purchase</option><option value="115">115 · after purchase</option></select></label><label>B has applied through <select data-applied><option value="105">105 · behind purchase</option><option value="120">120 · past purchase</option></select></label><label>Retained history starts at <select data-retained><option value="90">90</option><option value="110">110</option></select></label></div>
 <p class="timeline">100: before purchase → 110: purchase commits → 115: after purchase</p>
 <div class="ranges"><section><p class="panel-title">A · stock range</p><p>Closed through 120<br/>Applied through 120</p><p data-a>At 100: P7 stock 1</p></section><section><p class="panel-title">B · order range</p><p>Closed through 120<br/><span data-progress>Applied through 105</span></p><p data-b>At 100: order 103 absent</p></section></div>
 <p class="answer" data-answer aria-live="polite">Whole snapshot at 100: stock 1 and no 103</p><p data-explanation aria-live="polite">Both replicas have the required state and retained versions. The coherent older answer excludes the entire purchase.</p>
 <p class="caption">An illustrative frontier model with ordered numbers, not wall-clock seconds or measured replica positions. Only P7 and order 103 are drawn; the real purchase also changes P3 and its two lines. A closed promise cannot substitute for unapplied data or discarded versions. Change one input at a time.</p>
</figure>
<script>
 const root=document.querySelector('[data-r46-snapshot]');
 if(root){const time=root.querySelector('[data-time]') as HTMLSelectElement,applied=root.querySelector('[data-applied]') as HTMLSelectElement,retained=root.querySelector('[data-retained]') as HTMLSelectElement;
 const draw=()=>{const t=Number(time.value),b=Number(applied.value),oldest=Number(retained.value),expired=t<oldest,lag=t>b;
 root.querySelector('[data-progress]').textContent=`Applied through ${b}`;
 root.querySelector('[data-a]').textContent=expired?'Required old version not retained':`At ${t}: P7 stock ${t<110?1:0}`;
 root.querySelector('[data-b]').textContent=expired?'Required old version not retained':lag?`Cannot certify the answer at ${t}`:`At ${t}: order 103 ${t<110?'absent':'present'}`;
 root.querySelector('[data-answer]').textContent=expired?'No snapshot: requested history is outside retention':lag?'No complete local answer at the chosen timestamp':`Whole snapshot at ${t}: stock ${t<110?1:0} and ${t<110?'no 103':'103 present'}`;
 root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=expired?'Catching up does not recreate discarded history. The operation must reject this timestamp or use a separately available retained copy.':lag?'A can answer its part, but B has not applied enough state. Do not combine A’s new stock with B’s latest available old order state. Wait or use a replica that can serve the chosen timestamp.':t<110?'Both replicas have the required state and retained versions. The coherent older answer excludes the entire purchase.':'Both replicas can answer the post-purchase view. Stock and order belong to the same snapshot.';
 };[time,applied,retained].forEach(el=>el.addEventListener('change',draw));draw();}
</script>
<style>
.snapshot{margin:2.5rem 0;font-family:var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.25rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:.8rem}figcaption>span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.5rem}.controls{display:flex;gap:.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:.8rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt)}label{font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);display:grid;gap:.35rem;flex:1}select{font:inherit;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.5rem;max-width:100%}.timeline{font:.85rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);border-bottom:1px dashed var(--color-text-secondary);padding-bottom:.8rem}.ranges{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.7rem}.ranges section{margin:0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary)}.ranges p{font:.85rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);margin:.7rem 0 0}.ranges .panel-title{font-weight:600;margin:0}.answer{font:600 .95rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);border:2px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.8rem}[data-explanation]{font:.9rem/1.55 var(--font-sans)}.caption{font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary)}@media(max-width:550px){.controls{flex-direction:column}.ranges{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
